{
  "id": "ss.relic.mirror",
  "name": "Mirror shell",
  "description": "A domed shell, steel-grey with a curved band of white light across its shoulder, and one spit meeting it and leaving again: the incoming line is the hive's magenta, the line going back out is your own green, and the two make a V whose point sits on the shell's surface with a spark where they touch. The bolt head is on the outgoing leg, because what leaves is the thing that matters — a spit that lands on you flies back out as yours. The dome is flat-based and lit from the upper left so it reads as a convex surface rather than a disc, and the shell is kept plain (no horn, no ridge) to stay clear of ss.relic.armor's beetle helm.",
